-- @ Description: Screen Space Shaders - the SSFX page of the game's own settings menu
-- @ Mod: https://www.moddb.com/mods/stalker-anomaly/addons/screen-space-shaders

--[[
	Built the way Call of Pripyat builds its advanced graphics page
	( ui_mm_opt_video_adv.script ): a scroll view, one template static per row, and the
	caption and its control inside that row. Every control carries an options_item entry in
	ui_mm_opt.xml, so the engine's own COptionsManager reads and writes the console variable -
	this file only places the controls, it never touches a value itself.

	No window is kept in a module-level variable. The page is owned by the options dialog
	through AttachChild and SetAutoDelete, so it dies with the dialog instead of waiting for
	the Lua state to be closed. The table below is plain data.

	Generated by _ssfx_work\menu_page_build.py together with the <ssfx> block of
	ui_mm_opt.xml and ui_mm_opt_16.xml - run it again rather than editing here.
--]]

-- { kind, name, lines of caption }
--   kind: "h" module heading, "n" note, "t" slider, "l" drop-down list, "c" check box
--   name: the node is "cap_" .. name, and the control "track_" / "list_" / "check_" .. name
local rows = {
	{ "n", "legend", 2 },

